id: pm-vcs-tracker-lenses
title: Explain native changes through tracker lifecycle dependency evidence and policy lenses
description: Opt-in read-only projections over immutable native VCS changes alongside ordinary field and text provenance. Core history retains ownership of tracker records.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T21:35:13.973Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T10:23:08.731Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Malformed tracker objects remain opaque; views never rewrite content; every semantic statement cites the original object/change.; Typed SDK and CLI with bounded TOON/JSON, typed refusals and remedies, README and example, non-git public tracker validation, targeted regressions and CI npm plus Bun release gates."
comments[16]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T21:35:19.901Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check against current CLI 2026.10.21 and package main 27e1d84: core history owns tracker event streams and lifecycle mutations; pm-context assembles present context, pm-graph projects graph queries, pm-memory owns memory workflows, pm-changelog produces release notes. None explains one immutable native change as tracker field deltas. Reuse annotatePath/changeProvenance, native conflict IDs, signature policy and bisect rather than duplicating them. New query compares selected change to first parent, never invokes Git or writes content. Open reconciliation PR items are excluded from this work. Dependencies remain pinned."
  "2026-10-21T21:44:03.043Z",codex-agent,"Implemented explainChange SDK and vcs explain with opt-in labels, first-parent semantics, exact immutable commit/object/path citations, scalar/digest summaries and explicit pagination. Canonical SDK parsing plus typed collection coordinates prevent malformed tracker interpretations. Unresolved fields retain ordinary provenance; native conflict metadata is reused. No Git subprocess or mutable tracker read on the query path. Targeted SDK, CLI harness, installed TOON/JSON, malformed, shallow, conflict, deletion and byte-preservation checks are passing. CI now runs the unchanged npm and Bun release:check gates for both Node matrix versions; local full suites remain delegated to CI because host CPU is saturated."
  "2026-10-21T21:47:33.879Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof on production TypeScript: disable only the semantic label selection, then node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^SDK lenses\" test/tracker-lenses.test.ts fails 0/1; bypass only the malformed-tracker opacity guard, then node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^malformed tracker\" test/tracker-lenses.test.ts fails 0/1. Both functions are restored. Tests import source directly, so a dist rebuild is not needed for either revert. Collection projections now expose exact entry indices and bounded target/path/command/log coordinates; duplicates retain their counts and order-only edits do not invent membership changes."
  "2026-10-21T21:48:26.634Z",codex-agent,"Public-data read-only acceptance: public pm-vcs snapshots ab9e92eb4911..27e1d84671fa copied into a fresh SDK tracker without Git. Source tip contains 147 items, 2175 history events, 300 files and 4381779 bytes. Query returned 799 statements in 40 pages at limit 20: lifecycle 68, dependency 17, evidence 496, policy 16, field 176, opaque 26. Maximum JSON page 14000 bytes; total repeated-page query time 9967.47 ms on the saturated host. Tracker digest stayed exact: 9a6b751ed89486b87b7849fcebd688fbbb27d4544d8fc379c9a964caf5170fa7. Opaque includes history/configuration and makes no corruption claim. Reproduction helper and exact public refs are documented; no source data or temporary paths are committed."
  "2026-10-21T21:49:23.874Z",codex-agent,"Local validation: npm run typecheck, npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run lint, npm run docstring and npm run duplicates pass. Linked pm test run passed 1/1 commands and 7/7 behavioral tests with zero failed/skipped/canceled/todo. Test-result persistence is disabled by existing project policy, so receipt is retained here. The source-level collection-order refactor removes unreachable duplicate presentation branches without changing behavior. New-module targeted coverage and final CI full gates are checked separately; no coverage threshold is changed."
  "2026-10-21T21:50:16.672Z",codex-agent,"Final-source receipt: targeted new-module coverage is 100% statements/branches/functions/lines with all 7/7 tests passing. Closed-at timestamps are included in lifecycle. The repeated public-window measurement remains 799 statements, 40 pages and maximum 14000 JSON bytes, now classified as lifecycle 71, dependency 17, evidence 496, policy 16, field 173, opaque 26. Latest query time is 5066.08 ms; timing is observational. The documented public-data receipt uses these final-source counts. No reconciliation item or historical stream was modified."
  "2026-10-21T21:57:45.103Z",codex-agent,"Review handoff: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/140 is ready for review and is the durable location for exact-head CI results and full-suite counts. Source commit 5ed3de08b66e7982a0b5dd5027da663d4164601d has CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/39682108338 and CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/39682107923. CodeQL and both Windows launcher checks have passed; Linux full npm and Bun gate outcomes are available through the PR checks. This handoff also consolidates the existing Without git README section and clarifies that conflict references live at source commit/path coordinates. Current CLI 2026.10.21 and sibling source search confirms changelog selection explanation is distinct from native VCS-change interpretation. Automated reviewer budget/configuration skips are missing review evidence, not approvals. Item remains in_progress and released for orchestrator verification; no merge, release, history rewrite or reconciliation-item mutation."
  "2026-10-21T22:04:11.294Z",codex-agent,"Initial Node 22 CI receipt was 1774/1776, with zero skipped/canceled/todo: self-host archive mismatch and stale production-file inventory (75 measured versus 74 expected). The archive blob address exactly matched the temporary label-revert source: the archive writer reads working bytes and had overlapped that proof. The later handoff archive was regenerated after restoration, and the committed operational-entry regression now passes 1/1. Corrected the explicit inventory to 75 without changing measured scope or thresholds. All runtime source remains unchanged; final archive generation is sequential after edits, followed by verification against the committed head. New-module coverage was 100/100/100/100 even in the failed run; audit-script deficits followed the early operational-test assertion and are not accepted as full coverage evidence."
  "2026-10-21T22:12:52.419Z",codex-agent,"Adversarial validation found a pinned-SDK gap: parsing preserves unknown risk values, malformed or missing link scopes and invalid dependency timestamps. Views now explicitly validate built-in risk/dependency kinds, recorded timestamps and project/global scopes before assigning any semantic label; unrecognized custom kinds stay opaque. Expanded real-record malformed cases pass. Removing only the scope guard makes node --test --test-name-pattern=\"^malformed tracker\" test/tracker-lenses.test.ts fail 0/1; source restored before build or archive generation. Six focused source tests pass and the final lens module remains 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Repeated public validation is unchanged at 799 statements, 40 pages, maximum 14000 JSON bytes and exact tracker hashes; latest measured time is 3932.03 ms. No SDK dependency bump or upstream issue was made."
  "2026-10-21T22:13:34.682Z",codex-agent,"Strict-validation final linked run passed 1/1 commands and all 7/7 tests, zero failed/skipped/canceled/todo, including the newly built installed CLI with no Git executable. Typecheck, test typecheck, build, targeted lint, docstrings and duplication checks pass. The exact-head CI result and full npm/Bun suite counts remain linked from PR 140; superseded checks are not final acceptance evidence. No further runtime edits are planned."
  "2026-10-22T09:36:53.505Z",pi-agent,"Review of PR 140 unresolved threads against head c0df1c35554ca91e54edf83f303be7ec75dbc8bb. Collection duplicate pairing is valid: ascending after-indices consumed with pop report an appended identical entry at entryAfter 0 instead of 1, while a trailing removal already reports entryBefore 1. Fix will pair from the front and assert both coordinates. The Bun workflow thread is being checked against the contracted npm and bun release:check gates before any workflow edit."
  "2026-10-22T09:41:56.163Z",pi-agent,"Revert proof for duplicate collection coordinates: restoring only the match consumption in collectionStatements from shift() to pop() makes node --test --test-name-pattern='^collection lenses' test/tracker-lenses.test.ts fail 0/1. The appended [file] to [file, file] assertion expected entryAfter 1 and observed 0. The trailing-removal assertion was not reached. Source was restored to front pairing immediately. The same command then passed 1/1. Tests import source, so the proof did not need a dist rebuild. The full lens file then passed 7/7, including the installed CLI case with no Git executable. Public-window statement counts are unchanged because this aligns duplicate indices without adding or dropping rows."
  "2026-10-22T09:42:12.394Z",pi-agent,"CI thread PRRT_kwDOToJT7M6vBSTC is not a defect in the contracted gate. The step already runs bun run release:check, the package-manager gate required beside npm run release:check. release:check is npm scripts, and coverage is c8 invoking node --expose-gc --test. No bunfig is present. With node already on PATH, bun run does not alias node to bun. A local script probe showed bun run executes system node with no Bun runtime version, while bun --bun aliases node to the bun binary. Forcing --bun would replace the Node and c8 coverage toolchain instead of running the unchanged release gate. The merge-base workflow had no Bun-runtime test job, so this is not a regression. No workflow edit."
  "2026-10-22T10:06:16.550Z",codex-agent,"Continuation review: remote head pulled; branch contains current main. Reviewed unpushed duplicate-coordinate commit as an untrusted draft and retained its front pairing plus bidirectional coordinate assertions. Both unresolved threads and every comment were read; latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. Superseding the prior Bun refusal: the unchanged package-manager gate alone does not exercise the new feature under Bun. Add explicit Bun execution of the complete tracker-lenses test file after the full Bun release gate, with a regression that executes the actual workflow block and requires a Bun runtime witness. Self-reviewed the full diff for duplicate matching and runtime-selector defects; collection matching is shared by all lenses. No other occurrence found."
  "2026-10-22T10:07:53.361Z",codex-agent,"Independent continuation revert proofs: changing only collectionStatements match consumption from shift() back to pop() makes node --test --test-name-pattern=^collection\\ lenses test/tracker-lenses.test.ts fail 0/1 (actual entryAfter 0, expected 1); restoring it passes 1/1. Removing only the explicit bun test command from the CI shell block makes node --test --test-name-pattern=^Bun\\ CI\\ gate test/dependency-refresh-workflow.test.ts fail 0/1 because the Bun witness is absent; restoring it passes 1/1. Both source/workflow restorations completed before any archive generation. Node workflow file passes 4/4, and bun test --timeout 120000 ./test/tracker-lenses.test.ts passes 7/7 under Bun 1.3.5, including packed CLI without Git. npm ci passes with zero vulnerabilities. Full release gates will use isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git config; no threshold changes."
  "2026-10-22T10:23:03.864Z",codex-agent,"Final implementation handoff for PR 140: linked pm test run passes 3/3 commands (7 lens tests, 1 duplicate regression, 4 workflow tests; zero failures/skips/cancellations). Explicit Bun runtime lens suite passes 7/7. Build passes; dist is ignored and not committed. Strict pm health passes after installing the same project pm-github 2026.10.4 as CI; only pre-existing stale-item and provenance-domain advisories remain, with no history edits. Both unresolved findings are fixed with independent failing-revert/passing-restoration proofs above. Full npm release check is running with isolated HOME and disabled global/system Git configuration; both full npm/Bun gates at unchanged 100% per-file thresholds are also required by CI at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/140/checks. That final-head check page is the authoritative complete gate receipt, not the older review-head results. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification; item stays in_progress, no thread replies/resolution, merge or release."
